<p>
  Shared state is a <code>Y.Map</code> with one key per cell
  (<code>"x,y"</code>) and a palette index as the value. Pick a color, then
  click or drag on the canvas, in two windows at once. Painting a cell is one
  <code>map.set</code>: two people painting different cells merge, and two
  people painting the same cell keep the last write, which is r/place's rule
  too. The server records each paint as a row and never looks inside it.
</p>
<p>
  The Ruby side reads the same map back with <code>read_map</code>. The
  panels under the canvas render it as a PNG in plain Ruby, with no browser
  or image library, and replay it from <code>y_document_updates</code>. This
  demo's channel is <code>DocumentChannel</code> with compaction turned off,
  so that table holds every paint since the room opened.
</p>
